# Main Window — Persist Size/Position Across Launches PRD

## Overview

- **Status**: Completed (PR #7 rebase-merged to main, 2026-07-23)
- **Created**: 2026-07-20
- **Updated**: 2026-07-23
- **Owner**: josephjang
- **Translations**: Korean companion at `feature-persist-window-bounds.ko.prd` (kept in sync 1:1)

## Problem Statement

Every launch, the main window opens at the built-in defaults (1400×800, centered on the primary
screen). A user who prefers a different size, position, or a maximized window has to re-adjust it
on every start. The overlay minimap already remembers its geometry between sessions; the main
window should too.

## Goals

- [x] Goal 1: On launch, the main window reopens with the **same size, position, and
      maximized state** it had when it was last closed.
- [x] Goal 2: The restored window appears **directly** at the saved geometry — no visible
      jump from the centered default position.
- [x] Goal 3: **First run** (or no saved geometry) keeps today's behavior: 1400×800,
      centered, normal state.
- [x] Goal 4: **Safe fallbacks** — if the saved geometry is invalid (corrupt data, or the
      window would be off-screen because a monitor was unplugged/rearranged), the app falls
      back to the default geometry instead of opening invisibly.

## Non-Goals (Scope Out)

- Other windows: the overlay minimap (already persisted) and modal dialogs (transient by design).
- Per-profile geometry: window bounds are a device preference, **shared** across PvP/PvE profiles.
- Per-monitor DPI edge cases beyond the off-screen fallback.
- Restoring a minimized state (closing while minimized reopens as a normal window).

## Requirements / Acceptance Criteria

- [x] R1 (round-trip): Resize/move → close → relaunch reproduces the same bounds; maximize →
      close → relaunch reopens maximized, and un-maximizing returns to the last normal bounds.
- [x] R2 (no flicker): The window is first shown at the restored geometry (no center-then-move).
- [ ] R3 (multi-monitor): A window closed maximized on a secondary monitor reopens maximized on
      that monitor while it is present; if that monitor is gone, the app falls back to defaults.
      *(off-screen fallback verified by DB edit; physical secondary-monitor check pending)*
- [ ] R4 (minimized/fullscreen close): Closing while minimized reopens normal at the last normal
      bounds; closing while F11-fullscreen reopens maximized with normal window chrome.
      *(minimized close verified; F11-fullscreen close pending — covered by design, not exercised)*
- [x] R5 (resilience): Corrupt or out-of-range saved values never prevent startup — defaults apply.

## Technical Decisions

| Decision | Rationale | Date |
|----------|-----------|------|
| Store one JSON blob (`Left/Top/Width/Height/IsMaximized`) under a single global `UserSettings` key (`app.mainWindowBounds`) via the existing generic settings accessors | Atomic (no mixed-session values), zero `SettingsService` changes, same precedent as the overlay minimap's `overlayMiniMap.settings` | 2026-07-20 |
| Global scope, not per PvP/PvE profile | Window geometry is a device preference, not game-mode state | 2026-07-20 |
| Restore bounds in the window constructor; apply Maximized at `SourceInitialized` | Constructor placement avoids the visible jump (R2); deferring Maximized until the HWND exists makes Windows maximize onto the monitor containing the restored bounds (R3) | 2026-07-20 |
| Save once on `Closing`, using `RestoreBounds` when not in the Normal state | Avoids continuous DB writes during drags; `RestoreBounds` keeps sane normal bounds behind a maximized/minimized close (R1/R4) | 2026-07-20 |
| Off-screen check: a usable slice of the title-bar strip must intersect the virtual screen | Cheap, dependency-free guard against unplugged/rearranged monitors (R3/R5) | 2026-07-20 |

## Implementation Plan

### Phase 1: Persist and restore main window bounds

- [x] Task 1.1: Restore saved bounds (with validation/fallback) before the window is shown
  - Files: `TarkovHelper/MainWindow.xaml.cs`
- [x] Task 1.2: Save bounds + maximized state on window close
  - Files: `TarkovHelper/MainWindow.xaml.cs`
- [x] Task 1.3: XAML defaults unchanged — they are the first-run/fallback geometry
  - Files: `TarkovHelper/MainWindow.xaml` (no change expected)

