## Completion Criteria

- [ ] All Goals and Requirements (R1–R5) met *(R3 physical multi-monitor + R4 fullscreen pending)*
- [x] Build green (`dotnet build`)
- [x] Automated guard: `WindowBoundsPersistenceTests` protect the save/restore/validation rules
      (incl. a simulated secondary-monitor case) against silent regressions
- [x] Automated e2e: `MainWindowBoundsE2ETests` launch the real app in an isolated Config dir
      and verify the full save→close→relaunch→restore loop on the actual window
      (filter out of quick runs with `dotnet test --filter Category!=E2E`)
- [x] Manual checks: first-run defaults; normal/maximized/minimized round-trips;
      off-screen and corrupt-value fallbacks (by editing `user_data.db`); dark title bar
      still applied (seen in screenshots); overlay minimap persistence untouched

## Risks & Mitigations

| Risk | Impact | Mitigation |
|------|--------|------------|
| Saved bounds point at a removed monitor → window opens off-screen | Medium | Visibility check against the virtual screen; fallback to defaults |
| Corrupt/hand-edited settings value breaks startup | Low | Parse/validate defensively; any failure falls back to defaults |
| Hard process kill skips the close-time save | Low | Accepted — same tradeoff as the overlay; at worst one session's adjustment is lost |

---

## Archive Info

- **Completed**: 2026-07-23 (PR #7 rebase-merged to main)
- **Summary**: Main window size/position/maximized state now persist across launches via a
  single `app.mainWindowBounds` JSON setting. Pure core extracted to
  `Services/WindowBoundsPersistence.cs`; guarded by 11 unit tests plus 6 e2e tests that
  launch the real app in an isolated Config dir (`TARKOVHELPER_CONFIG_PATH`).
- **Actual vs Planned**: Implementation matched the 3-task plan. Scope grew beyond it in
  testing: the pure-core extraction, the unit suite, and the Win32-driven e2e harness were
  added during the session rather than planned up front.
- **Lessons Learned**: Restore in the constructor / apply Maximized at `SourceInitialized`
  is the flicker-free, multi-monitor-correct split. Close-time-only saving is acceptable
  for geometry. Launching via `dotnet TarkovHelper.dll` bypasses the admin manifest and
  makes real-app e2e practical.
- **Follow-up Items**: R3 physical secondary-monitor and R4 F11-fullscreen-close checks
  when the hardware/scenario is at hand (design-covered; fallbacks verified). The e2e
  harness in `MainWindowBoundsE2ETests.cs` is slated for extraction/reuse by
  `feature-persist-map-view-state.prd`.
